Z||000000||Brian||12-02-2000||03:10 PM||||The clutch in my 85 GT project car was not completely dis-engaging. Grinding going into reverse & 1 & 1/2" play at the top of the clutch pedal were the symptoms. <P>After following Ed Park's method (http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html#clutch) the clutch is working like new!<P>Along the way I discovered an upside down & worn "banjo", but the real fix was the bleeding.<BR>There are only two things I did a bit differently. First I removed the slave to jam the pushrod back into the cyl.<BR>The darn heat shield wouldn't let me do it any other way (at least easily) & this bleed became a simple one- man job being unbolted from the block.<BR>Second, the very last thing I did was give it one more conventional bleed & got one last little bubble of air.<P>Measured at the slave pushrod the throw went from a grinding low of 7/16" to a smooth trouble free 7/8".<P>My hat's off to Ed !!!<P>Regards,<BR>Brian<BR>||||reg||7
